@startuml settings_propagation
!include ../dark-theme.puml
' Revised 2026-07-12: mandatory DDC timeout and per-monitor dwell projection
title Settings change propagation - who reacts to AppSettings.Changed

actor User
participant "Settings page partials\n(<Name>Page.cs: General/Flyout/TrayIcon/\nMonitors/Hotkeys/Environmental/Theme)" as PG
participant "AppSettings\n(AppSettingsCommon base)" as AS
participant "TrayXmlFileStore\n(settings.xml on disk)" as ASD
participant "App.OnSettingsChanged\n(central funnel)" as AOC
participant "MonitorService\n.OnSettingsChanged" as MS
participant "NightLightProvider\n.OnSettingsChanged" as NLP
participant "BrightnessFlyout\n.OnSettingsChanged" as BF
participant "EnvironmentalCurveService" as ECS
participant "BrightnessSettingsWindow\n(SettingsWindowCommon)" as SW
participant "Tray icon + tray menu\n(TrayIconPresenter,\nTrayMenuController)" as TIM
participant "GlobalHotkeyService" as GHS
participant "PDBSymbolResolver" as PDB

== Edit on a settings page ==

User -> PG : edit any setting
PG -> AS  : property setter (SetField)\n-> RaiseChanged + implicit save request
PG -> SW  : Save()
SW -> AS  : RaiseChanged() only when no setter raised it\n(lists and nested objects)
SW -> ASD : settings.Save()  (explicit: always writes)
note right of PG $TINT_NEUTRAL
  One Changed per edit. Implicit saves
  (setters, RequestSave, the save at exit)
  are coalesced by the store and only
  happen while Autosave is on; the
  settings window's Save() is explicit
  and always writes. Color overrides
  (NullableThemeColor) raise Changed
  through the base's color callbacks.
end note

== Multicast to subscribers ==

AS -> AOC : Changed
AS -> MS  : Changed
AS -> NLP : Changed
AS -> BF  : Changed (while the flyout exists)

== App.OnSettingsChanged - central funnel (posted to the UI thread) ==

AOC -> AOC : ApplyThemeVariant + ApplyThemeResources
AOC -> PDB : ApplyPDBDownloadTimeout\n  (NightLightPDBDownloadTimeoutSeconds)
AOC -> MS  : WriteCooldownMs (= BrightnessUpdateRateMs)\nValidationDwellMs
AOC -> TIM : ApplyTrayIconScrollSettings
AOC -> GHS : Apply(_settings.Hotkeys)\n  (re-register WM_HOTKEY bindings)
AOC -> AOC : tooltip delay on open windows
AOC -> TIM : ApplyTrayIconSettings (style, colors)
AOC -> BF  : NotifyUpdateStateChanged()
AOC -> TIM : keep-warm policies (flyout slot, tray menu)\n-> RequestTrayRefresh()
note right of TIM
  TrayMenuController invalidates the
  warm tray menu on settings and theme
  changes by itself.
end note

== MonitorService side reactions ==

MS -> MS : _display.OperationTimeoutMs\n  = DDCOperationTimeoutMs
MS -> MS : Clamp production timeout to >= 500 ms;\nnon-positive values use safe default
MS -> MS : ApplyDDCTimingOverridesToExisting()\nValidationDwellMs / BrightnessDwellMs\nnegative inherits global timing
alt MonitorIdentityStrategy changed
    MS -> MS : Refresh()  (re-key every MonitorInfo)
else strategy unchanged
    MS -> MS : ApplyNameOverridesToExisting()\nResortMonitors()
end

== NightLightProvider side reactions ==

alt NightLightFallbackMode changed
    NLP -> NLP : InvalidateBackendCache()\nGetCachedBackend()  (re-probe Registry vs SettingsHandler)
else mode unchanged
    NLP -> NLP : skip (only fallback mode matters)
end

== BrightnessFlyout side reactions ==

BF -> BF : UpdateMasterFromEnabledIndividuals()\n  (DynamicIconBrightnessTracking, MasterSliderMode)\n  only when the recomputed master value differs, so an\n  unrelated save does not reset curve auto re-engage
BF -> NLP : GetStrength() / IsEnabled() readback\n  -> sync NightLightMonitor.Brightness\n  (handles InvertNightLightSlider flip)
BF -> BF : Docking.RedockIfUndockingDisabled()\n  (AllowFlyoutUndock turned off)
BF -> BF : UpdateAllCurveStopwatchVisibility\n+ QueueRebuild() (Common rebuild scheduler;\n  held while a slider or editor is in use)
BF -> ECS : _curveService.Start() + Evaluate()\n  (pull EnvironmentalCurveTickIntervalMs,\n   EnvironmentalOffsetMode, smoothness, location)

== Settings window chrome ==

SW -> SW : appearance cards (theme style, rounded corners,\ncolors, animations) rebuild the window\n(RebuildCurrentPage)

note over AOC
  UpdateCheckService does not subscribe to Changed;
  the About page's update cards act on the service directly.
end note

== Out-of-band saves (no RaiseChanged) ==

note over NLP $TINT_AMBER
  NightLightProvider may persist
  NightLightLastNonZeroStrength without
  RaiseChanged, so subscribers don't fan
  out for what is effectively a sticky cache
  field used only by the next toggle-on.
end note

note over AS $TINT_BLUE
  The settings window saves explicitly on every page
  edit. Known displays live in displays.json
  (KnownDisplaysStore), not in settings.xml.
  Writes go through the Common store: one writer,
  atomic temp+replace (AtomicFile), failures logged.
end note

note over ECS $TINT_AMBER
  ECS does NOT subscribe to AppSettings.Changed.
  Setting edits made during a closed-flyout window
  (e.g. EnvironmentalCurveTickIntervalMs, smoothness,
  lat/lon) won't take effect on the curve service
  until the flyout's OnSettingsChanged pulls the
  live values into the service via
  Start() + Evaluate().

  ECS DOES subscribe to SystemEvents.TimeChanged
  for DST / clock changes - those reset the curve's
  date-keyed cache (_cachedShifted*) so the next
  Evaluate observes the new wall-clock anchor.
end note

note over BF $TINT_AMBER
  BrightnessFlyout.OnSettingsChanged does NOT
  re-read the curve enable flags from AppSettings.
  The flyout setter is the canonical writer (steps
  1..9 sync on UI dispatcher). Any out-of-band
  AppSettings writer (none today) would not
  propagate to the service / flyout mirrors.
end note

note over AOC $TINT_RESOLVED
  Hotkey edits take effect immediately:
  AOC calls GHS.Apply on every settings
  change, so users don't need a hotplug or
  app restart for new bindings to register.
end note

@enduml
